My bags are very heavy now.
I stop near a small tea stall.
The market is very crowded.
I am very tired.
"Dada, give me one cutting chai, please," I say.
"Yes Madam, I will give it right away," the vendor says.
He gives me a hot cutting chai.
"How much is it?" I ask.
"Ten rupees," the vendor says.
I have loose change in my purse.
I take out coins from my purse.
I give him exactly ten rupees.
The small tea glass is very hot.
I slowly drink the tea.
The tea is sweet and tasty.
I watch the people in the market.
Now I feel very good.
